{"id":1795025,"retrievedAt":"2026-10-12T20:30:33.643Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"}],"homepage":"","id":1795025,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["IN"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Here Lies Makhfi","overview":"Here Lies Makhfi is a portrait of the 17th century Indian princess Zeb-un-nissa who wrote Persian poetry under the nom de plume Makhfi (the hidden one). Daughter of the Mughal emperor Aurangzeb, Zeb-un-nissa is an enigmatic figure in Indian history and her poetry is our only window into her life. The film positions Zeb-un-nissa's poetic expression within the contemporary zeitgeist of neglect and selective amnesia, tracing her work through three people – an actress recounting the memory of playing Zeb-un-nissa, a young Iranian woman reading her poetry for the first time, and a government official attempting to locate her now-lost grave. And thus, it is in rummaging in neglected buildings, abandoned homes and decaying manuscripts that we discover the remains of an unrecorded history.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/zESN9RGCTfyXUOCSCnOaxLo0xyN.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"2025-11-01","revenue":0,"runtime":68,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Persian","iso_639_1":"fa","name":"فارسی"},{"english_name":"Hindi","iso_639_1":"hi","name":"हिन्दी"},{"english_name":"Marathi","iso_639_1":"mr","name":""},{"english_name":"English","iso_639_1":"en","name":"English"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Here Lies Makhfi","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":3308049,"known_for_department":"Directing","name":"Prachee Bajania","original_name":"Prachee Bajania","popularity":0.4756,"profile_path":null,"credit_id":"6accbc96f84cd7353abfc493","department":"Directing","job":"Director"},{"adult":false,"gen